  data: {
    LLM: "Learn the hand rankings thoroughly - 7-5-4-3-2 is the nuts\nUnderstand that straights and flushes are bad\nRemember aces are always high (bad cards)\nDrawing more than one card is risky due to pairing probability\n\nWhen drawing to a five-card hand, seldom draw more than one card\nIf you draw two cards, you'll make a pair about 50% of the time\nChance of making 9-high or better is never more than 25% when drawing two\nPosition matters - act last for maximum information\n\nTriple draw strategy: can draw more cards on first draw, but stand pat or draw one on final draw\nBluffing with pat hands (no draw)\nReading opponents' draw patterns\nPot odds calculations for drawing decisions\nMixed game strategy when Deuce-to-Seven is one of several games",
